fdisk
Usage: fdisk [-uls] [-C CYLINDERS] [-H HEADS] [-S SECTORS] [-b SSZ] [-t PARTTYPE] DISK

Change partition table

	-u		Start and End are in sectors (instead of cylinders)
	-l		Show partition table for each DISK, then exit
	-s		Show sizes in kb for each DISK, then exit
	-b 2048		(for certain MO disks) use 2048-byte sectors
	-T PARTTYPE	Force 'dos' partition if 'gpt' also present
	-C CYLINDERS	Set number of cylinders/heads/sectors
	-H HEADS	Typically 255
	-S SECTORS	Typically 63
